Review Report Summary ({case_id})
I. Incident Overview: Starting from {date} {time}, a total of 31 base stations across 2 prefecture-level cities in one area reported cell out-of-service and S1 link anomalies in succession, with 31 sites and 97 cells affected cumulatively.
II. Timeline:
{time}-08 The network management system issued batch script {batch}, performing batch modification of neighbor cell parameters and power parameters for the 31 base stations;
From {time}+00:03, the above base stations began reporting out-of-service alarms intensively;
At {time}+00:19, it was determined to be related to the script, and rollback was executed;
At {time}+00:30, services of all base stations were restored and alarms were cleared.
III. Evidence: Comparison of network management configurations before and after the change shows that only this script introduced differences; during the same period, there was no optical cable construction and no power outage records in the area, received optical power was all within the normal range of -12 ~ -16 dBm, there were no hardware alarms, and peak utilization was 46%.
IV. Conclusion: Caused by a recent configuration change, not a hardware or optical path problem; the engineer on duty needs to participate on site in confirming the rollback.
Note: The shift change on the duty roster for {date} has been confirmed and is unrelated to this incident.

